.TH cmprestart 1  "USER COMMANDS"
.SH NAME
cmprestart \- Compare two restart files for LPJmL and check for identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cmprestart
[\-q] \fIrestartfile1\fP \fIrestartfile2\fP

.SH DESCRIPTION
Program compares the numerical data of two LPJmL restart files and checks for identity. In case of a difference the variable name and the two values are printed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-q
Print only the number of different values.
.TP
.I restartfile1
Name of restart file.
.TP
.I restartfile2
Name of restart file to compare.
.SH EXAMPLE
.TP
Compare two restart files:
.B cmprestart
restart1.lpj restart2.lpj
.PP
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B
cmprestart
returns a zero exit status if the two restart file have been compared.
Non zero is returned in case of failure.

